                <pb facs="0771" n="669" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg669"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 847/146.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counsellor of the Legation of
                            Panama to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Panama</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-10-06"><hi rendition="#italic">October 6,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to advise you that the
                    inauguration of Don Jose Domingo de Obaldia as President of the Republic of
                    Panama occurred at the capital of the Republic on the 1st instant, and that the
                    following named have been constituted members of the new cabinet, to wit: Don
                    Jose Augustin Arango as secretario de relaciones exteriores; Don Ramon A Valdes
                    as secretario de gobierno y justicia; Don Carlos A Mendosa as secretario de
                    hacienda; Don Eusebio A Morales as secretario de instruccion publica.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Nelson
                    Cromwell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
